{"issue_id":3021,"body_hash":"","kind":"other","test_cases":[],"reproducer":"# Run on XPU (4 GPUs)\nexport ZE_AFFINITY_MASK=0,1,2,3\ntorchrun --nproc_per_node=4 test_alltoall_single.py\n\n# Test different dtypes\ntorchrun --nproc_per_node=4 test_alltoall_single.py --dtype bfloat16","error_message":"torch.distributed.all_to_all_single produces corrupted data on 4x Intel Arc Pro B60 (XCCL).","traceback":"","notes":"torch.distributed.all_to_all_single returns corrupted output on 4x Intel Arc Pro B60 via XCCL while the functional-collectives equivalent works, impacting Ulysses attention in sglang-diffusion."}
